--- body ---
## Context

The current Exp 1 figure (`fig_direct_p1_base.pdf`, produced by
`aedist.plot_method_convergence` with `--methods direct`) packs each
model's recalled plants to the left of its row. Two models recalling the
same number of plants look identical even when they recall *different*
plants. The reader cannot tell which gold-list assets each model misses.

Replace the left-packed dots with a boolean matrix: rows = (model, run),
columns = gold-list plants in a fixed order (e.g. by status × capacity).
A filled cell means "this model recalled this plant"; an empty cell means
"miss". The vertical alignment makes coverage patterns immediately legible
— famous plants form dense columns; obscure plants form sparse ones.

## Relevant files
- `src/aedist/plot_method_convergence.py` — current figure producer
- `data/reference/vietnam_thermal_v1.csv` — gold list ordering source
- `experiments/outputs/exp1_batch2/*.record.json` — per-run hits
- `report/inputs/generated/fig_direct_p1_base.pdf` — committed handoff artifact

## Spec refresh (author-ratified 2026-06-05)

- **Rows (Y): every run** — all models x all 5 reps, NOT the
  min/median/max trio of `_select_min_median_max`. Row ordering: same as
  the existing figure (models by effective parameter count; within a
  model, reps by run number).
- **Columns (X): the reference plants** ordered by **status group, then
  capacity descending** — the column bands then line up with the status
  difficulty table (0434) that follows the figure in the annex.
- **NEW — FP panel on the left**: the 40 most common false positives
  across all runs, sorted by occurrence count descending, **ties
  shuffled with a fixed seed** (rebuild-stable). Shows matcher/list
  issues and hallucinating runs. Visually separate from the reference
  columns (gap or rule); FP marks use the red FP convention (0403).
- **Placement: a NEW annex** holding this figure together with the
  status difficulty table (0434) — companion material;
  `fig_direct_p1_base.pdf` stays in the main text.
- **Cite from the Discussion** (author 2026-06-05): reference the annex
  figure in the future-work paragraph of the Discussion section, where
  information fusion, truth discovery, and coherence between runs and
  between models are mentioned — the matrix previews that research
  direction (tickets 0396-0400: row coherence, internal/external
  composites, latent-truth PU fusion, run-quality gate,
  capture-recapture; design notes in
  docs/2026-06-03-list-fusion-litreview.md). Each column is a plant
  observed by many noisy runs — exactly the input object of truth
  discovery and capture-recapture estimation.
- **Own mart view, no side-output** (author 2026-06-05): the figure
  derives its per-(run x plant) recognition from the mart/records
  layer directly. The status table (0434) derives the same data
  independently — consistency by common cause (shared mart), never by
  one script consuming the other's output file. If a shared derivation
  helper is warranted, it is library code in `src/aedist/` that both
  import.
- **No hardcoded plant count**: read the reference at build time
  (caption count via macro). NOT blocked on 0413; after v2 adoption the
  DAG rebuild regenerates the figure.

## Actions
1. Sibling script `src/aedist/plot_exp1_matrix.py` (different visual
   primitive than plot_method_convergence; reference path from config,
   0419 ratchet).
2. Implement spec above; wire the figure in render.mk.
3. Create the new annex (figure + slot for 0434's table); keep
   `fig_direct_p1_base.pdf` in place.
4. Add the Discussion future-work citation (fusion / truth discovery /
   inter-run, inter-model coherence) pointing to the annex.
5. Commit the generated PDF as handoff artifact.

## Test
`tests/test_plot_exp1_matrix.py` — golden test on synthetic fixture:
- N models × M plants matrix, half hit half miss
- Verify the script produces a non-empty PDF
- Verify the derivation helper returns a boolean matrix matching the
  input hits (unit-test the library function, not a file)

## Verification
- [x] Figure produces a boolean matrix with plants aligned vertically,
      all 5 reps per model
- [x] Columns ordered status group then capacity desc; documented in
      caption
- [x] FP panel: 40 most common FPs, count-sorted, seeded tie-shuffle
- [x] No side-output: derivation via library helper, no intermediate
      file consumed by 0434
- [x] Generated PDF committed as handoff artifact, included in a NEW
      annex shared with 0434's table
- [x] Discussion future-work paragraph cites the annex figure (fusion /
      truth discovery / inter-run, inter-model coherence preview)
- [x] `make check` passes (only the @slow claude-cli smoke fails, on
      exhausted API credits — environmental, not in this diff)

## Invariants
- Clean-room writing build — no `uv run` in `make report` / `make slides`
